\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  O Jesus Christ, the Son of God
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 How come about this your suffering?
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj What have you done for these soldiers
\par to handle you with much disgrace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Your own natives and your kingsmen
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Disliked you so with much hatred
\par How have you offended Judah
\par to cause them to hate you so much?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My father God has allowed it;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Before such a thing could happen
\par the cost of salvation is great
\par there's no other way except this.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I, the thoughts my Lord mediate
\par      With pitying, tears His suff'ring mourn
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 I have to do my God's own work
\par who sent me into this world.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Master, do not let me forget
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 This your great suffering ever
\par until the day when I'll go through
\par the gates of death and come to you.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

